          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_22",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("After securing the help of the two lich-mages, the party returned to Knalga."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_23",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hamel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Och, that was a piece o’ good work, lad, getting both the lich-mages and Stalrag on our side. Now let’s plan our way to bringing Rakshas down..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_24",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The lich-mages sent forth gryphons to scout out the number, formation and deployment of the orcish forces, and to seek allies as well."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_25",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("One day a gryphon came screeching into the caves with the news that a large elvish force approached from the east. Messages were quickly dispatched to the elves asking their purpose. The haughty reply was that their purpose was none of any dwarf’s or human’s business, and that all would be well-advised to stay in their holes when the elves passed near."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_26",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Before the humans and dwarves could respond to this message, another gryphon arrived with the news that the orcs were holding an elvish sorceress prisoner in the castle of Bitterhold, less than a day’s march to the northwest. The castle had attracted notice because it had been recently rebuilt and manned by a force known to include some of the hardiest and toughest of veteran orcs."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_27",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("Gryphons and a picked force of human woodsmen were sent out that very night, and less than two days later managed to ambush an orcish messenger on the road out of Bitterhold. The messenger was carrying a ransom demand to the elves — for the sorceress was, in fact, a princess of the highest rank."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_28",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            text: _("The leaders met in council, considering what to do..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_29",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ This kidnapped princess explains a great deal. It is not easy to draw the elves out of their forests."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_30",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hamel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Aye, lad. Her kin will have come either to do battle or pay ransom. By the looks of things, they’ve busked themselves for either."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_31",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Arthian.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Pah! Who cares? Let the elves and orcs chop each other into mincemeat. It will just make things easier for us."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_32",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Stalrag.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Hah! Yer brain has rotted awa’ entire. Think on it, skull-head, what would happen if the elves dinna’ fight and pay the ransom instead?"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_33",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Arthian.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Do you want to die, dwarf?"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_34",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Father_Morvin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Peace, peace! If you two want to kill something, there are plenty of orcs outside."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_35",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Father_Morvin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ But you do have a point, Stalrag. That ransom will buy more troops and weapons for the orcs, and that is bad news for us."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_36",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ I think we have a chance to make some new allies here..."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_37",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hamel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Allies? I take it we’re to go to them and ask them to join us in return for our help in rescuing their princess? You heard their message — those elves have got their noses so high in the air they canna’ see over them. They wouldna’ ally themselves with the likes o’ us."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_38",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Of course we won’t do that. As a matter of fact I think it’s best that we don’t say anything to the elves at all."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_39",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Stalrag.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Why d’ye say that?"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_40",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Well, suppose we do join up with the elves — assuming they will let us — and we make a combined raid on the fortress, what will the orcs most likely do when the ransom slips from their grasp?"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_41",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hamel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Kenning the way of orcs, they’d kill the princess, especially if it seems the rescue ha’ any chance of succeeding."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_42",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Exactly. On the other hand, if we raided the fortress while the orcs were talking ransom with the elves, the orcs might hesitate just long enough for us to free her."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_43",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hamel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Hmmm... I think you’ve the right of it, lad. Most orcs being thicker than a wood-knot, I’d lay odds on Rakshas giving strict orders that she not be touched without his direct word on the matter."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_44",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ But it would be unwise to trust that the orcs will stay stupid forever. If we do go ahead with this raid, we are going to have to be in and out like lightning."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_45",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Stalrag.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ My Shinsplitters be invaluable for this kind o’ job. They be braw warriors and dinna stop their assault till either they or their opponent lie dae. Nae a fortress can stand against them."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_46",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Arthian.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Ha ha, I like this plan! Once we get our hands on this little sorceress the elves will be forced to do whatever we want them to!"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_47",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Father_Morvin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Remember, Ro’Arthian, we need willing allies rather than resentful lackeys that would turn on us at the first chance. If we rescue their princess, the elves may yet choose not to help us, but that is a risk we’ll have to take."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_48",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Sister_Thera.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Elves are deeply honor-bound, especially in matters that touch their kin. If we rescue the princess, I am certain the deed will not go without reward."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_49",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ And at the very least, the orcs will not be able to raise troops with ransom money they don’t have."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_50",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Arthian.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Bah... weak, soft humans. Have it your way if you must."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_51",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Hamel.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ So it shall be, Tallin, I’ll hold the caves here while you and Stalrag’s Shinsplitters fare to Bitterhold. The orcs still haven’t given up their attack on our southern tunnels."),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "story_52",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: _("portraits/Tallin.webp"),
            text: _("<span color='#bcb088'><b></b></span> _ Then to arms, men!"),
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "loyal_53",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:make_loyal",
            units: "Tallin,Atul,Eryssa",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "clock_54",
        on: "start",
        children: [
          {
            tag: "set_variable",
            name: "turn_limit",
            value: 18,
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "objectives",
        side: 1,
        victory: _("Rescue the Princess Resist for as long as you can"),
        defeat: _("Death of Tallin Death of Ro’Arthian Death of Ro’Sothian"),
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_1",
        on: "prestart",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "breaking_the_chains.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "elvish-theme.ogg",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:play_music",
            file: "nunc_dimittis.ogg",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_2",
        on: "prestart",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:capture_village",
            side: 1,
            cells: "",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_3",
        on: "prestart",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:capture_village",
            side: 2,
            cells: "",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_4",
        on: "prestart",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:recall_unit",
            id: "Father Morvin",
            unit: "Father Morvin",
          },
          {
            tag: "hook",
            name: "command:recall_unit",
            id: "Sister Thera",
            unit: "Sister Thera",
          },
        ],
      },
      {
        tag: "event",
        id: "ev_5",
        on: "start",
        once: true,
        children: [
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "narrator",
            portrait: "wesnoth-icon.png",
            text: _("Upon emerging from the mouth of a hidden tunnel near the fortress, Tallin and his men surveyed the scene before them."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Tallin",
            text: _("There’s the fortress of Bitterhold. A grim and impressive pile indeed..."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Supporter",
            text: _("They have dammed the river to make a moat for their castle."),
          },
          {
            tag: "message",
            speaker: "Ro'Arthian",
            text: _("Are we here to sight-see or to rescue this blasted sorceress? If you really want to sight-see, then check out that orcish encampment south of us."),
          },
          {
